--
-- Tests for bc-interpretation-time.l4: the time words the Act defines and the moments it fixes
-- (Interpretation Act (British Columbia), RSBC 1996, c. 238, ss 20, 25.1 and 29 "month" and "year").
--
-- Expected values were decided from the text before the first run:
--   * "month" is "a period calculated from a day in one month to a day numerically corresponding
--     to that day in the following month, less one day" (s 29): a month that begins on 15 January
--     ends on 14 February;
--   * "year" is "any period of 12 consecutive months" (s 29): twelve of those months in a row;
--   * a person reaches an age "at the beginning of the relevant anniversary of the person's birth
--     date" (s 25.1);
--   * an appointment begins at the beginning of the day it is effective and ends as s 20(4) says.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `bc-interpretation-time`

GIVEN d  IS A DATE
      h  IS A NUMBER
      mi IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Pacific Time moment`
`test: Pacific Time moment` d h mi MEANS
    `Pacific Time moment` WITH `calendar day` IS d, `hour of the day` IS h, `minute of the hour` IS mi

§ `s 29 month`

#ASSERT `s 29 the last day of a month that begins on a day` (YMD 2026 1 15) EQUALS YMD 2026 2 14
#ASSERT `s 29 the last day of a month that begins on a day` (YMD 2026 1 1) EQUALS YMD 2026 1 31
#ASSERT `s 29 the last day of a month that begins on a day` (YMD 2026 2 1) EQUALS YMD 2026 2 28
#ASSERT `s 29 the last day of a month that begins on a day` (YMD 2024 2 1) EQUALS YMD 2024 2 29
#ASSERT `s 29 the last day of a month that begins on a day` (YMD 2025 12 15) EQUALS YMD 2026 1 14
#ASSERT `s 29 the last day of a month that begins on a day` (YMD 2024 1 29) EQUALS YMD 2024 2 28
-- The following month has no day numerically corresponding to the 31st (or the 29th, 30th): the
-- text does not say what then. s 25.3(3) is written for periods "expressed in relation to a
-- reference day" and is not applied to this definition (NOTES, fork F-month-def).
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 29 the last day of a month that begins on a day` (YMD 2026 1 31)
        BECAUSE "s 29 month: the following month has no day numerically corresponding to the day the month begins on"
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 29 the last day of a month that begins on a day` (YMD 2025 1 29)
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 29 the last day of a month that begins on a day` (YMD 2026 3 31)
#ASSERT `s 29 the day on which the month following a month that begins on a day begins` (YMD 2026 1 15) EQUALS YMD 2026 2 15

§ `s 29 year and calendar year`

-- A calendar year is 12 consecutive months beginning on 1 January: it ends on 31 December.
#ASSERT `s 29 the first day of the calendar year` 2026 EQUALS YMD 2026 1 1
#ASSERT `s 29 the last day of the calendar year` 2026 EQUALS YMD 2026 12 31
#ASSERT `s 29 the last day of the calendar year` 2024 EQUALS YMD 2024 12 31
-- Any other year is 12 consecutive months from the day it begins.
#ASSERT `s 29 the last day of a year that begins on a day` (YMD 2026 7 1) EQUALS YMD 2027 6 30
#ASSERT `s 29 the last day of a year that begins on a day` (YMD 2025 3 15) EQUALS YMD 2026 3 14
#ASSERT `s 29 the last day of a year that begins on a day` (YMD 2023 3 1) EQUALS YMD 2024 2 29
#ASSERT `s 29 the last day of a year that begins on a day` (YMD 2024 3 1) EQUALS YMD 2025 2 28
-- A year that begins on the 29th, 30th or 31st runs into a month with no such day.
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 29 the last day of a year that begins on a day` (YMD 2026 1 31)
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 29 the last day of a year that begins on a day` (YMD 2024 2 29)

§ `s 25.1 Calculation of age`

-- Born 2000-05-17: reaches 18 at the beginning of 2018-05-17.
#ASSERT `s 25.1 the day a person reaches an age expressed in years` (YMD 2000 5 17) 18 EQUALS YMD 2018 5 17
#ASSERT NOT (`s 25.1 a person has reached an age on a day` (YMD 2000 5 17) 18 (YMD 2018 5 16))
#ASSERT `s 25.1 a person has reached an age on a day` (YMD 2000 5 17) 18 (YMD 2018 5 17)
#ASSERT `s 25.1 a person has reached an age on a day` (YMD 2000 5 17) 18 (YMD 2018 5 18)
-- Born on 29 February: the anniversary exists in a leap year.
#ASSERT `s 25.1 the day a person reaches an age expressed in years` (YMD 2004 2 29) 4 EQUALS YMD 2008 2 29
#ASSERT `s 25.1 the day a person reaches an age expressed in years` (YMD 2000 2 29) 20 EQUALS YMD 2020 2 29
-- ... and in a year with no 29 February the text does not say which day it is.
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 25.1 the day a person reaches an age expressed in years` (YMD 2000 2 29) 18
        BECAUSE "s 25.1 does not say which day is the anniversary of a birth on 29 February in a year that has none"
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 25.1 a person has reached an age on a day` (YMD 2000 2 29) 18 (YMD 2018 3 1)

§ `s 20 Appointments of officers`

-- An appointment begins at the beginning of the day it is effective (s 20(3)).
#ASSERT `s 20(3) the moment an appointment begins` (YMD 2026 3 10) EQUALS `test: Pacific Time moment` (YMD 2026 3 10) 0 0

-- (a) the instrument specifies the day it terminates: the beginning of that day.
#ASSERT `s 20(4) the moment an appointment ends` (`The appointing instrument specifies the day the appointment terminates` (YMD 2026 6 30)) EQUALS `test: Pacific Time moment` (YMD 2026 6 30) 0 0
-- (b) it does not: the end of the last day of the term.
#ASSERT `s 20(4) the moment an appointment ends` (`The appointing instrument does not specify the day, and the appointment has a last day of its term` (YMD 2026 6 30)) EQUALS `test: Pacific Time moment` (YMD 2026 7 1) 0 0
-- (c) an enactment terminates it and specifies the day: the beginning of that day.
#ASSERT `s 20(4) the moment an appointment ends` (`An enactment terminates the appointment and specifies the day the termination is effective` (YMD 2026 5 15)) EQUALS `test: Pacific Time moment` (YMD 2026 5 15) 0 0
-- (d) an enactment terminates it and does not specify: the beginning of the day the enactment is made.
#ASSERT `s 20(4) the moment an appointment ends` (`An enactment terminates the appointment and does not specify the day the termination is effective` (YMD 2026 5 20)) EQUALS `test: Pacific Time moment` (YMD 2026 5 20) 0 0
-- (e) the same enactment appoints another person to the office: when the new appointment begins.
#ASSERT `s 20(4) the moment an appointment ends` (`The same enactment terminates the appointment and appoints another person to the same office` (`test: Pacific Time moment` (YMD 2026 5 20) 0 0)) EQUALS `test: Pacific Time moment` (YMD 2026 5 20) 0 0
